odgins-May","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_11020","person_slug":"steph-hodgins-may","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sue Lines","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10782","person_slug":"sue-lines","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tammy Tyrrell","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_11012","person_slug":"tammy-tyrrell","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tim Ayres","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10946","person_slug":"tim-ayres","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tony Sheldon","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10944","person_slug":"tony-sheldon","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tyron Whitten","party":"One Nation","person_id":"tvfy_11060","person_slug":"tyron-whitten","vote":"no"},{"name":"Varun Ghosh","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11017","person_slug":"varun-ghosh","vote":"no"},{"name":"Wendy Askew","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10914","person_slug":"wendy-askew","vote":"no"}],"name":"Motions — Universal Periodic Review","noes":30,"question":"David Shoebridge I seek leave to move a motion relating to the UN's Universal Periodic Review as circulated. Leave not granted. Pursuant to contingent notice standing in the name of Senator Waters, I move: That so much of the standing orders be suspended as would prevent me moving a motion to provide for the consideration of a matter, namely a motion to give precedence to a motion relating to the Universal Periodic Review. It is quite extraordinary that the Albanese Labor government's response to the UN periodic review about Australia's human rights record, which recommended some 332 changes to Australia's human rights laws, was to reject 204 recommendations. And we only found out about this because the response was published on a fairly hard-to-identify part of the UN's website. Sue Lines Senator Shoebridge, I remind you that you've moved a suspension motion, so that's what you need to address—why the matter is so urgent that the parliament needs to suspend. David Shoebridge This is urgent because it has only just been found out today; we only found out today that the Albanese Labor government have said to the world that they do not support raising the age for criminal prosecutions. We only found out today that the Albanese Labor government have said to the world that they want to keep putting ten-year-old kids into jail, kids who still have their milk teeth. We only found that out today. We only found out today that there are more than 200 recommendations to fix Australia's human rights record that the Albanese Labor government have said no to. Do you know what one of them is? One of them is to introduce a human rights act—a human rights act that would protect the human rights of all Australians. It may not be to the flavour of Gina Rinehart. It may not be to the flavour of Labor's corporate donors to a human rights act in place, but it sure as heck— Sue Lines Senator Shoebridge, I remind you again you need to address why the matter is urgent that you need to susp","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-10564","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2026-07-01/12"}
